{
  "rationale": "This is the first iteration, so there is no race telemetry or integration feedback yet. I chose a conservative baseline that should be easy for the Integrator to control and that gives clear evidence back. Five sensors in a 4 cm line spread across the front of the robot give enough lateral coverage to see a 25 mm tape at up to about ±2 cm offset, with 12 mm footprints overlapping slightly so the reading changes smoothly as the line moves. Sensors sit 6 cm ahead of the axle so the controller sees the line before the wheels reach it, which matters at the speeds needed to finish in 3 s. Wheel track 0.12 m and wheel radius 0.03 m give moderate turn authority and a speed range that can reach about 1.5 m/s. Mass 0.8 kg keeps inertia low enough for quick corrections while leaving some traction margin. Body width 0.12 m keeps the off-track limit at 0.06 m. Under the contract, any body width up to about 0.19 m leaves that limit at 0.06 m, so the width does not need to be larger. Expected result: a completed run on the oval with few line-loss events. The main risk is oscillation on the slalom, which would show up in steering_oscillation and max_error.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.06},
      {"x": 0.01, "y": 0.06},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.06},
      {"x": -0.01, "y": 0.06},
      {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.06}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "intent": "Baseline geometry: five 12 mm sensors in a 4 cm front-mounted line, spaced 1 cm, with a 6 cm lookahead ahead of the axle. Symmetric left-right, so a weight vector proportional to sensor x (for example +2, +1, 0, -1, -2) gives a signed steering signal. Chosen for a low-risk platform the Integrator can tune, not for peak speed. Next iteration, I will adjust sensor spacing, lookahead and wheel track based on how the controller handles the oval and s-bend.",
  "feedback_request": {
    "questions": [
      "Does the 1 cm sensor spacing with 12 mm footprints give a usable, monotonic signal across the ±2 cm range, or do the middle sensors saturate or drop out when the tape is centred?",
      "Is the 6 cm lookahead helping or causing overshoot on tight bends? Would a shorter lookahead be easier to control?",
      "Is the 0.12 m wheel track enough to turn tightly on the slalom without wheel slip, or is it too narrow?",
      "Is the 0.8 kg mass a problem for reaching about 1.5 m/s average speed, or is there spare traction?",
      "Which sensor positions or weights would you change if you were free to choose them?"
    ],
    "measurements_next": [
      "rms_error", "max_error", "steering_oscillation", "line_loss_events", "completion_time", "progress", "completion", "control_effort"
    ]
  },
  "learning": "No race data yet. Hypotheses to test: (1) a lookahead of about 6 cm is enough to let the controller react before the line is lost, (2) 5 sensors at 1 cm spacing are enough lateral resolution without excess noise sensitivity, (3) 0.12 m track and 0.8 kg mass allow the speed needed to finish in 3 s without slip-induced error."
}
